 the fusion product of two evaluation modules. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nco.combinatorics - Order polynomial of shifted double staircase - MathOverflow (https://mathoverflow.net/questions/343005/order-polynomial-of-shifted-double-staircase/363162)\nciteturn3search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.1 years ago; Crawled: last month; And let $P$ be the poset corresponding to $\\lambda$ (i.e., the poset on the boxes of $\\lambda$ viewed as a shifted shape, with $u \\lessdot v$ if the box $v$ is directly right of or directly below the box $u$). ... Discrete Mathematics & Theoretical Computer Science (DMTCS). ... 2, Research Paper R9, 24 p. ...   * This conjecture is now mentioned in arxiv.org/abs/2006.01568. ... Tri Lai and I proved this conjecture, using the techniques from the theory of lozenge tilings.\n\nedited Nov 29, 2019 at 18:12\n\nasked Oct 3, 2019 at 1:02\n\nSam Hopkins♦\n\n26.8k 6 6 gold badges 119 119 silver badges 218 218 bronze badges\n\n  * What is the order polynomial of a staircase (and of a reflected staircase)?\n\n–  Ilya Bogdanov\n\nCommented Oct 3, 2019 at 9:04\n\n  * @IlyaBogdanov: I included this information. I also updated to include a conjectured formula for the shifted double staircase order polynomial, since based on my data it is very simple.\n\n–  Sam Hopkins ♦\n\nCommented Oct 3, 2019 at 14:30\n\n  * This conjecture is now mentioned in arxiv.org/abs/2006.01568.\n\n–  Sam Hopkins ♦\n\nCommented Jun 5, 2020 at 11:20\n\n## 1 Answer\n\nSorted by:\n\n[Select]\n\n[Input]\n\n6\n\n[Input]\n\nTri Lai and I proved this conjecture, using the techniques from the theory of lozenge tilings. Indeed, this result is almost already proved by Ciucu in https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.02021. We just need to allow slightly more general parameters for the \"flashlight\" region of the triangular lattice which he considers- and the techniques he developed there suffice to do that. -------------------------------------